# Keep line endings consistent on every platform.
#
# soap-journal runs inside a Linux container even on Windows and macOS
# (Docker Desktop runs a Linux VM). The container's bash entrypoint must have
# LF line endings or it won't boot. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh to CRLF
# on clone and break the container with a cryptic "bad interpreter" error.
# Forcing LF here removes that whole class of problem for non-technical users.

# Normalize text files to LF in the repo and on checkout, on every OS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts MUST stay LF or the Docker entrypoint won't start.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
